# Canonical identity for the project's history.
#
# Commits were made from a few different machines and setups over time, which left the
# same person recorded under five name/email combinations. GitHub already collapses these
# into one contributor because it matches on the account's verified addresses, but local
# tooling does not: `git shortlog`, `git log --author`, and anything counting contributors
# would otherwise report five people.
#
# This file is display-only. It rewrites nothing, changes no commit, and breaks no link —
# git simply reads through it when showing an author. The alternative, rewriting history
# to correct the recorded names, would change every commit id and permanently break the
# commit links in CHANGELOG.md and in the published releases.
#
# Format: Canonical Name <canonical@email>  Recorded Name <recorded@email>

CyKiller <cykiller@msn.com>  CyKiller <Cykiller@msn.com>
CyKiller <cykiller@msn.com>  Aaron Johnson <Cykiller@msn.com>
CyKiller <cykiller@msn.com>  CyKiller <devway83@gmail.com>
CyKiller <cykiller@msn.com>  StepStitch <devway83@gmail.com>
